WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:26.340
[Music]

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.420
[Narrator:] Good food. Attractive. Tasty. Nutritious and safe.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.620
Good food, the end product of skilled craftsmen,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:45.420
working in one of the world's biggest industries.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:51.280
Chicken salad, pork chops, spinach, and corn.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.680
The simple foods on this tray required real craftsmanship in their preparation.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.120
Let's see just when the cook started this meal.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.400
Let's turn back the clock to yesterday morning when the pork loins were delivered.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.600
The other foods were already on hand.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:10.220
Pork loins and the turkey.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.840
As usual, each item was carefully inspected.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:18.300
That's the only way to be sure of what you're buying.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.340
The pork loins were government inspected and stamped.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.700
That means a lot to any good restaurant name.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:30.400
But not all foods are stamped.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.160
This turkey for example.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:36.000
In this case, the restaurant must depend upon a reliable supplier.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:40.740
It’s the best anyone can do where government inspected poultry is not available.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:47.200
Government-inspected meat, certified shellfish, grade A pasteurized milk,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.920
and clean vegetables and fruits.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.320
To serve safe food, a restaurant must buy safe food,

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:56.640
and then be sure to store it properly.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:04.800
[Music]

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:08.080
This completes delivery of the food for tomorrow's menu.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.200
It's inspected and stored. Preparation of part of the meal is already underway.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:18.960
Dinner today and lunch tomorrow.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.400
Making things work out right is a scheduling job.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.240
Any last minute changes?

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:27.760
Chicken salad, chicken pie, pork chops, fish...

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.600
No, everything just as planned.

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:37.700
Here's a good example of planning or scheduling, or whatever you want to call it.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.440
These are for tomorrow's chicken salad.

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:44.240
Cooked today and refrigerated overnight,

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.740
the chicken will be cooled when the salad is made.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:53.300
That’s important because cold food inhibits the growth of bacteria.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:03:00.080
He's working on a schedule, not only using his hands, but using his head.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.440
Here we are next morning.
 Back to today.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.200
The day we're going to make and serve the chicken salad.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.420
This is the way to begin the job.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:11.340
He's particular about clean hands.

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:13.760
Everyone has to be, in a kitchen.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.280
Let’s see about the salad.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:17.780
Looks like the chicken is almost boned.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:19.980
Now here is the important thing.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.380
He's working with cold chicken.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:28.560
Cold not only keeps the chicken from spoiling, 
it makes the meat firmer and easier to work.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:30.080
Faster to work.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:35.280
Time-saving, and time is important in an operation where the possibility of contamination

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.780
is so obviously present.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:47.600
You've heard of time and motion studies but it looks like our cook has been associated

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.000
with some of that work.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:04:28.560
[Music]

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:36.400
It’s easy to see how important it is for cooks to keep their hands clean.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.440
Everything is planned, everything in hand.

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:41.600
Clean, cold food,

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.900
clean equipment, and the know-how.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:48.680
Who says this cook isn't a craftsman?

00:04:48.780 --> 00:05:02.480
[Music]

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.680
Clean food and equipment, and the know-how.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.040
He's still working with cold, really cold chicken.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.640
That's important.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:15.440
And he's keeping it cold until served.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.440
He knows his business.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:27.040
Pork chops: clean cold meat and clean equipment.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:29.600
Clean hands, clean equipment,

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.960
and cold food, an unbeatable team.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:37.760
He's taking no chances of spreading contamination.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:42.080
Good food, clean equipment, and the know-how.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.800
Someone has to keep everything working on schedule.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:57.760
[Music]

00:05:57.760 --> 00:05:59.680
How 'bout the spinach, Joe?

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:02.080
Will ya get three packages from the deep freeze?

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:04.280
Okay.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:15.920
[Music]

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:19.040
Proper storage depends on people and equipment.

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.520
This is a good piece of equipment.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:26.940
But credit for the way that food is stored in the chest belongs to kitchen workers.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:41.200
[Music]

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:47.220
Yes, food preparation is an orderly job as long as the people doing the work know their business.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:58.800
Good equipment and the know-how.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:01.840
A good cook is a deliberately clean cook.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:04.640
He is conscious of timing and coordination.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:07.900
As well as nutrition and taste.

00:07:08.020 --> 00:07:51.040
[Music]

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:54.320
Good equipment and intelligent people.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:57.020
No overcrowding in this storeroom.

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.640
And no invitation to rats and insects either.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:10.240
What's this? A leaking can, spoiled food.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:15.720
Put it aside for the moment, but get it out of the kitchen as soon as possible.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.920
The corn in these cans is clean.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.000
Let’s keep it that way.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.040
The top of the cans may have gathered dust.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.080
Wipe them off with a clean cloth.

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:36.960
And you can be sure that this can opener is clean.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:42.080
If it were not, it would be an ideal breeding place for bacteria.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:51.040
Good clean food.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.920
And it’s just as clean as it looks.

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:56.320
Must be getting close to lunchtime.

00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:58.960
Let’s check our pork chops.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:04.240
Undercooked pork, pink pork, can cause trichinosis.

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:08.720
According to schedule, our pork chops should be done.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.720
White pork, it's thoroughly cooked.

00:09:12.720 --> 00:09:16.480
And now that it's ready to serve, the job has only started.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:20.080
Let’s keep the food the way it should be kept until served.

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:24.280
Keep it hot or keep it cold, or don't keep it long.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:28.720
Any good cook has heard this a thousand times.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:31.840
Looks like we're back at our starting point doesn't it?

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:36.240
Chicken salad, pork chops, spinach, and corn. Remember?

00:09:36.320 --> 00:09:40.000
This tray of food was just ready to go to our customers earlier in the picture.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.100
While they're eating, let’s look around the kitchen.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:50.000
It’s a busy place.

00:09:50.160 --> 00:09:53.600
Customers are waiting and more are coming in every minute.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:58.080
That’s the restaurant business, it comes in rushes.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:06.000
There's no place for inefficiency in a busy kitchen.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.000
Each job is important.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.960
Every job requires skill.

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:14.620
And they're all hard work.

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:33.880
[Music]

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:39.520
But all the skill and hard work that goes into preparing a good meal is not wasted.

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:47.240
These people recognize and appreciate good food and the craftsmanship that goes into preparing it.

00:10:47.300 --> 00:10:50.640
They're completing a successful meal from everyone's standpoint.

00:10:50.640 --> 00:10:55.600
Theirs, the waitress's, the cook's, and the management's.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.840
This may be their first meal here but it won't be their last.

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:00.960
They'll be back again.

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.920
Maybe tomorrow or maybe next week.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.240
No matter when it is, they'll find safe food.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:13.180
Because safe food isn't an accident here, it’s a policy.

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:40.000
[Music]

00:11:40.640 --> 00:11:43.840
No, safe food isn't an accident here for a lot of reasons.

00:11:43.920 --> 00:11:48.400
The cook plans his meals so that he has little in the way of leftovers.

00:11:49.160 --> 00:11:52.480
The few that he does have, he stores properly.

00:11:55.020 --> 00:11:59.920
And like most skilled craftsman, he is sensitive to his surroundings.

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:03.880
He sees that his stove and other equipment is kept clean.

00:12:04.520 --> 00:12:07.640
Everything is planned and supervised in this kitchen.

00:12:07.960 --> 00:12:11.120
A really skilled craftsman doesn't leave anything to chance.

00:12:15.120 --> 00:12:20.560
This cook has knowledge and ability, and the way he uses them everyday

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:24.840
demonstrates his skill in craftsmanship.

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.120
His count is the symbol of his perfection.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.420
He is proud of it and he has the right to be.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:45.160
[Music]

